   "body": "## Art direction after review (PR #1384, head `1c05111`, Opus APPROVE round 3)\n\nThis replaces the caption table of my proposal above; the direction itself (the `:o` poster language) is unchanged.\n\n![The phone frames with placeholders](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/blob/1c05111/docs/assets/appstore/art-direction.jpg?raw=true)\n\n| # | Screen | Caption | Changed in review |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Catégories | Tout HFR, / en natif. | |\n| 2 | Topic reader | Des topics / enfin lisibles. | |\n| 3 | Composer (formatting bar open) | Gras, citation, / spoiler, lien. | « sans balises » was false for the default composer, which edits BBCode |\n| 4 | Private messages | Vos MP, / sous le pouce. | |\n| 5 | Themes | Clair, sombre, / rétro 5250. | |\n| 6 | Large screen | Grand écran, / deux colonnes. | Only at the iPad and iPhone Duo inner sizes: a phone in portrait shows one column, so the phone sets have six frames |\n| 7 | Offline reading | Le topic / dans le tunnel. | |\n\nRule added to the README: a caption says only what its capture shows and the default build does.\n\n**Waiting for the operator:** the direction, the screens and the captions; whether the listing ships iPad; whether the Duo set is provided now.\n\n**For the final-render session** (two optional details of the last review, not pushed): word the README as « a failed render changes no image » (a failed `--sheet` step can leave the old contact sheet next to new images), and write the temporary `sheet.html` inside `.staging/`. Also to check on the Mac: whether simulator captures carry a Display P3 profile.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
